@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `.env` loader now strips a leading `export `, removes matching single/double quotes, splits on the first `=` only (the old `split("=")` crashed on values containing `=`, such as the endpoint URL), and skips lines without `=`. Added `redact()`.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor` prints `KEY = value  [env|.env|default]` for every setting. Unset values show `(not set)`.
+- Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are masked to a 3-char prefix + `****`, because the output is meant to be pasted into tickets.
+- `docs/SUPPORT.md`: runbook now points at `doctor`. It previously said tickets must contain the full API key. I did not follow that, so please confirm with billing.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 4 tests OK (they cover quotes, `export`, `=` in values, env precedence, and doctor run as a subprocess).
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo against the real `.env`: all 5 settings listed, quotes and `export` handled, the endpoint keeps its `?region=eu&mode=live`, the token and secret are masked, and REGION shows `[default]`.
+- `python -m payhook check` prints `ok`.
+
+## Not verified
+- The env-over-`.env` source label in `doctor` is only covered indirectly by the unit tests. My manual run with `PAYHOOK_REGION=us` was blocked by the sandbox.
+- Not handled: inline `# comments` after values, escape sequences in double quotes, multi-line values.
+- The README wasn't changed.
